        "original_id": "e3c61571-bbc3-56ce-b24c-c386395a1e52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium\n- Plant families: Fabaceae, Iridaceae, Mirbelioids\n- People: James Edward Smith\n- Places: Australia, tropical Africa, southern Africa\n\nFacts:\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to Bossiaea, another genus within the Mirbelioids.",
